30
00:04:27,424 --> 00:04:32,064
They might also be not perfectly flat, and I'll say a little bit in a moment about that.

31
00:04:34,318 --> 00:04:37,984
And we also take measurements of the system itself.

32
00:04:38,064 --> 00:04:46,820
So we measure some fiducials in the system, and we use this to actually track the changes in the machine itself over time.

33
00:04:47,246 --> 00:04:51,344
So the machine can warm up, can cool down, and so on.

34
00:04:52,304 --> 00:05:00,304
Then the business end of the machine is the actual exposure using a radical.

